---
import NoteFigure from './NoteFigure.astro';
---

<NoteFigure
  label="Reverse process"
  title="The training target knows x₀; the generation model does not"
  caption="Reconstructed from the reverse-chain arrows on page 40 and the three-state diagram on page 42. For an interior step t ≥ 2, the extra x₀ input belongs to the tractable training posterior, not the learned generation transition. The panel layout and explicit input labels are editorial additions. Arrows indicate conditioning and sampling direction, rather than an observed trajectory."
>
  <div class="reverse-panels">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 340 450" role="img" aria-labelledby="ddpm-reverse-generation-title ddpm-reverse-generation-desc">
      <title id="ddpm-reverse-generation-title">Generate a sample by following learned transitions from noise to data</title>
      <desc id="ddpm-reverse-generation-desc">The model starts with x T sampled from a standard Gaussian. It reaches a noisy state x t, samples the next state x t minus one using p theta conditioned on x t, and continues to x zero. The network sees x t and the timestep but has no original clean image.</desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="ddpm-reverse-generation-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="arrowhead" /></marker>
      </defs>
      <text x="170" y="25" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-title">Generation: T → 0</text>
      <rect x="104" y="48" width="132" height="46" rx="4" class="node" />
      <text x="170" y="77" text-anchor="middle" class="symbol">x<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">T</tspan> ∼ N(0, I)</text>
      <path d="M 170 100 V 139" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-reverse-generation-arrow)" />
      <text x="196" y="127" class="muted">earlier steps</text>
      <rect x="130" y="145" width="80" height="44" rx="4" class="node" />
      <text x="170" y="174" text-anchor="middle" class="symbol">x<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t</tspan></text>
      <path d="M 170 195 V 261" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-reverse-generation-arrow)" />
      <text x="192" y="225" class="formula accent">p<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">θ</tspan>(x<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t−1</tspan> | x<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t</tspan>)</text>
      <text x="192" y="249" class="muted">one learned step</text>
      <rect x="130" y="267" width="80" height="44" rx="4" class="model-node" />
      <text x="170" y="296" text-anchor="middle" class="symbol">x<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t−1</tspan></text>
      <path d="M 170 317 V 358" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-reverse-generation-arrow)" />
      <text x="196" y="344" class="muted">continue denoising</text>
      <rect x="104" y="364" width="132" height="44" rx="4" class="model-node" />
      <text x="170" y="393" text-anchor="middle" class="symbol">generated x₀</text>
      <text x="170" y="437" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">No original x₀ is supplied to the model.</text>
    </svg>

    <svg viewBox="0 0 340 450" role="img" aria-labelledby="ddpm-reverse-target-title ddpm-reverse-target-desc">
      <title id="ddpm-reverse-target-title">During training, the known clean example supplies a Gaussian posterior target</title>
      <desc id="ddpm-reverse-target-desc">For a timestep greater than or equal to two, the noisy state x t and known clean example x zero both enter the fixed forward posterior q of x t minus one given x t and x zero. Its posterior mean and variance form the target. Only x t and t enter the learned network, producing mu theta. Training compares target and model distributions through KL divergence.</desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="ddpm-reverse-target-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="arrowhead" /></marker>
        <marker id="ddpm-reverse-model-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="accent-head" /></marker>
      </defs>
      <text x="170" y="25" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-title">Training: compare one reverse step</text>
      <rect x="24" y="51" width="126" height="45" rx="4" class="node" />
      <rect x="190" y="51" width="126" height="45" rx="4" class="node" />
      <text x="87" y="80" text-anchor="middle" class="symbol">noisy x<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t</tspan></text>
      <text x="253" y="80" text-anchor="middle" class="symbol">known x₀</text>
      <path d="M 87 102 V 133 H 126 V 159" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-reverse-target-arrow)" />
      <path d="M 253 102 V 133 H 214 V 159" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-reverse-target-arrow)" />
      <text x="170" y="122" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">both conditions</text>
      <rect x="29" y="165" width="282" height="70" rx="4" class="node" />
      <text x="170" y="191" text-anchor="middle" class="formula">q(x<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t−1</tspan> | x<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t</tspan>, x₀)</text>
      <text x="170" y="219" text-anchor="middle">Gaussian target · t ≥ 2</text>
      <path d="M 87 102 H 9 V 278 H 40" class="model-arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-reverse-model-arrow)" />
      <rect x="46" y="253" width="248" height="55" rx="4" class="model-node" />
      <text x="170" y="276" text-anchor="middle" class="accent">network input: x<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t</tspan> and t</text>
      <text x="170" y="299" text-anchor="middle">predict μ<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">θ</tspan>(x<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t</tspan>, t)</text>
      <path d="M 317 202 H 326 V 372 H 258" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-reverse-target-arrow)" />
      <path d="M 170 314 V 345" class="model-arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-reverse-model-arrow)" />
      <rect x="86" y="351" width="166" height="42" rx="4" class="comparison" />
      <text x="169" y="378" text-anchor="middle" class="formula">KL(target ∥ model)</text>
      <text x="170" y="422" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">x₀ helps define the training target.</text>
      <text x="170" y="443" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">It is absent from the network input.</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
</NoteFigure>

<style>
  .reverse-panels { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
  svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; max-width: 400px; margin-inline: auto; }
  text { fill: var(--ink); font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 15px; }
  .panel-title { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; }
  .symbol { font-size: 21px; }
  .formula { font-size: 17px; }
  .subscript { font-size: 11px; }
  .muted { fill: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
  .accent { fill: var(--accent); }
  .node { fill: var(--paper); stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1.3; }
  .model-node { fill: var(--paper); stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.3; }
  .comparison { fill: var(--paper); stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 1.3; }
  .arrow, .arrowhead { fill: none; stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .model-arrow, .accent-head { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  @container (max-width: 580px) { .reverse-panels { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2rem; } }
</style>
